 The game harness uses a disposable profile and dummy audio, and needs a graphical
 display to construct Options. It checks discovery, decoder rollback, mood changes,
 selector actions, mute state and saved preferences.
+
+Runtime encoding now uses FFmpeg/libopus at 48 kbps VBR stereo, directly from the rendered 48 kHz PCM. Run the existing render and install commands; Vorbis and libsndfile are no longer required for installation. Regenerate installed-sets.json and render-info.json when installing.
